# Type and icons

On every UI change, match the neighbor screen, then check this table. Use `ThemeStore` fonts and colors. Do not invent hex, `Color.primary`, or a one-off purple/blue for row icons.

## Titles

| Surface | Font | Color |
|---|---|---|
| Soft-cover, onboarding, alerts, celebrations | `display(32)` + `.tracking(-0.4)` | `mainText` |
| Sheet chrome | `sheetTitle()` → `display(24)` | `mainText` |
| In-page section (`Suggestions`, …) | `display(24)` | `mainText` |
| Empty state | `display(22)` + `.tracking(-0.4)` | `mainText` |
| Settings group header | `bold(18)` | `mainText` |
| Settings / form row title | `regular(16)` or `regular(17)` | `mainText` |

## Subtitles

| Surface | Font | Color |
|---|---|---|
| Soft-cover, coach, Nice work, Suggested words, First words | `regular(16)` | `secondaryText` |
| Onboarding page line | `regular(16)` | `mainText.opacity(0.75)` |
| Empty state | `regular(15)` | `secondaryText` |
| Row body / bullet | `regular(14)` | `mainText` or `mainText.opacity(0.85)` |
| Caption / footer / hint | `regular(13)` | `secondaryText` |
| Settings trailing value | `regular(15)` + `lineLimit(1)` | `secondaryText` |

## Icons

| Kind | What |
|---|---|
| Soft-cover / empty hero | Sticker. SF fallback only: `iconAccent` |
| Row, toggle, settings, menu | SF Symbol via `MenuSymbol` (18 / frame 28) or the same metrics. Color: `mainText` |
| Nice work / Suggested words rows | SF Symbols, `mainText`, not a sticker, not `accentPurple` |
| Rainbow row (`iconBlue`, `iconGreen`, …) | Only where that settings row already uses it |
| Delete | `accentRed` |
| CTA | `mainAccentColor`. Home PRO sparkle: `accentBlue` |
| Add / Add all plus | `AddPlusIcon` — SF `plus`, 14pt bold. Do not inherit the button’s Poppins font |

Do not tint row icons to match the hero. Do not darken `accentPurple` / `accentBlue` for bullets.

## Before done (UI)

Re-read the diff: every new `Text` / `Image(systemName:)` / `StickerSymbol` uses a row from this table. If a screen already has a title + subtitle pair, copy that pair — do not mix `display(32)` with a 13-pt gray subtitle or a purple row icon.
